    "description": "Vanaha Verdant is a residential project by Shapoorji Pallonji in Vanaha, the group's integrated township of about 1,000 acres off the Pune\u2013Bengaluru highway near the Oxford Golf Resort, in Lavale village (Mulshi), marketed as Vanaha Bavdhan. Towers 3 and 4 have just launched; MahaRERA registers them as Vanaha Verdant Elm I & II (PR1260002500649), with Image Realty Private Limited as the promoter and a proposed completion date of 31 July 2032. The project has four towers of 30 to 31 floors above stilts on about 6.5 acres, around a forest garden of about 1.5 acres planted with native species. Homes are 2 BHK of 868 and 874 sq ft from \u20b91.05 crore, 3 BHK of 1,171 sq ft from \u20b91.55 crore, and 2+2 BHK Jodi homes of 1,736 sq ft from \u20b92.20 crore, laid out as 3.5 or 4.5 BHK with four decks. The 45-plus amenities include a 25 m lap pool, a kids' pool and spa pool, a watch tower, a 500 m elevated cycling track, a breezeway, a party lawn, a barbecue court and outdoor work desks, with a jogging track, a multiplay court, a futsal court, a yoga lawn and a half basketball court on the roof of the multi-level car park. A 64 m retail promenade lines the entrance. The township includes a 150-acre golf course, and FLAME University and Symbiosis International University's Lavale campus are nearby.",
